  "services.coturn.actions.title": "Actions",
  "services.coturn.actions.help": "Restart & verify preserves configuration and needs confirmation, not fresh identity verification. Apply & verify and Repair use protected recreation and may require fresh identity verification. All are bounded server-owned operations; none connects or disconnects a Matrix stack. External client reachability requires a separate test.",
  "services.coturn.actions.restrictedHelp": "Protected Coturn mutation and credential-dependent checks are disabled in this host-native execution context. Switch to Container development for production-shaped verification or protected service operations.",
  "services.coturn.hostNative.openPortainer": "Open Portainer",
  "services.coturn.hostNative.showHelp": "Why are these controls limited?",
  "services.coturn.hostNative.hideHelp": "Hide host-native recovery help",
  "services.coturn.hostNative.helpTitle": "Host-native Coturn recovery",
  "services.coturn.hostNative.helpDescription": "Direct Source and Managed Local intentionally do not receive the owner-only Coturn secret or protected configuration authority. Containerized Development and Production keep that protected authority so MEM can perform credential-dependent verification, Restart & verify, and Repair without exposing the secret to host-native developer processes.",
  "services.coturn.hostNative.portainerSetupTitle": "Portainer first-time setup",
  "services.coturn.hostNative.portainerSetupDescription": "A fresh Portainer 2.39.5 installation requires a one-time setup token before the first administrator can be created. Portainer prints that token to its server logs. The username defaults to admin but can be changed, and the password must be at least 12 characters.",
  "services.coturn.hostNative.portainerSetupToken": "Run this on the Docker host and copy the value after setup_token= into Portainer's Setup token field. The token is one-time use.",
  "services.coturn.hostNative.portainerSetupTimeout": "The first administrator must still be created within five minutes. If Portainer has timed out, restart only Portainer, reopen it immediately, then run the token command again to use the newest setup token.",
  "services.coturn.hostNative.portainerSetupBoundary": "Portainer owns the setup token and administrator credentials. MEM displays only the retrieval command; it does not read, store, proxy, or recover the token or Portainer administrator password.",
  "services.coturn.hostNative.troubleshootTitle": "When Coturn misbehaves in local development",
  "services.coturn.hostNative.troubleshootDescription": "Inspect the Coturn logs and Docker state first. For development-only recovery, use the server-approved Portainer handoff above or host-side Docker commands to start, stop, or restart mem-coturn. Switch to Container development when you want MEM's production-shaped protected recovery workflow.",
  "services.coturn.hostNative.manualBoundary": "Manual Docker or Portainer mutations are a development escape hatch. They bypass MEM's durable maintenance journal and post-operation functional verification, so they are not the normal production recovery path.",
  "services.coturn.hostNative.portainerUnavailable": "Portainer is not currently available through MEM. Use host-side Docker tooling or restore the Portainer support runtime.",
  "services.coturn.externalIp.label": "External/public IP",
  "services.coturn.externalIp.placeholder": "Optional, for example 203.0.113.10",
  "services.coturn.externalIp.help": "Leave empty for automatic detection on each Coturn start, or enter the public IP for a NAT deployment. Edits are not saved by typing or by a plain restart: use Apply & verify. Clearing an existing IP also needs confirmation.",
  "services.coturn.externalIp.automatic": "Automatic detection",
  "services.coturn.externalIp.pending": "Network setting changed — not applied yet. Review and apply it explicitly.",
